{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unheedful-custodial-bluebottle","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\nA write-side transient runner-FS fault aborts store git operations that route through\n`gitutil.run_git_write`, because that seam's transient-retry family covers only READ-side\nsignatures. The same fault is already recognised and retried on the `git add` path, so the\nstore self-heals in one place and red-lights CI in another.\n\nObserved on change 1702 (2026-08-13, run 31670466731): the s3 doctor's `git commit-tree`\nfailed with `error: unable to create temporary file: No such file or directory`, aborting\n`tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py::test_heal_folds_into_the_ref_from_a_detached_head_tracker`\nwith `S3DoctorConflict: could not build the merge commit folding\nrefs/rebar-doctor/<sha> into tickets`. One shard only (ubuntu py3.11); ubuntu py3.12,\nubuntu py3.13 and macos py3.13 passed the identical code, and all 9 tests in the file pass\nlocally.\n\n## Evidence the signature is already known-transient\n`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:183` defines\n`_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS = (\"unable to create temporary file\", \"failed to insert into\ndatabase\", \"unable to index file\")`, and the comment above it\n(`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:175`) documents this exact fault: the loose-object temp\ncreate under `.git/objects/` returning ENOENT on Linux (\"unable to create temporary file: No\nsuch file or directory\") or EINVAL on macOS, \"a transient filesystem hiccup, NOT a data fault\n— the identical add succeeds on retry (a Gerrit `recheck` on the same patchset passes)\",\nrecorded under bugs vocal-dip-robin / brainy-floral-globefish.\n\n## Evidence of the gap\n`gitutil.run_git_write` (`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:472`) composes two retry loops:\n`_with_index_lock_retry` (`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:339`) for git lock conflicts, and\n`_with_transient_head_retry` (`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:440`) for READ faults. The latter\nmatches only `_TRANSIENT_HEAD_MARKERS = (\"could not parse head\",)`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:405`) and `_TRANSIENT_OBJECT_MARKERS = (\"bad object\",)`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:417`). Neither matches a write-side temp-file ENOENT, so\n`run_git_write` returns the failure on the first attempt.\n\n`_with_transient_add_retry` (`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:197`), which DOES match it, is\ncomposed only into `event_append._git_add`. Every other caller of the shared seam — the s3\ndoctor (`src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py:47`, deliberately routed through `run_git_write` by\ncommit aa61323613 after three CI failures of the same bundle step), compaction, and the\nclaim/transition writers — is unprotected against this fault class.\n\n## Approach\nMove the write-side transient family into the shared seam so every store git caller inherits\nit, rather than growing a second private copy. The retried operations are already required to\nbe idempotent — `run_git_write`'s docstring states that precondition, and `commit-tree`,\n`add` and `commit` all satisfy it (content-addressed writes, re-run on the same state).\nKeep the corrupt-object exclusions the existing markers document: real damage must still\nsurface once the bounded retries are spent.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` — recognise the write-side temp-file signatures in the shared\n  transient retry.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — have `_git_add` reuse the shared family instead of its\n  own copy, so there is one definition.\n- `tests/unit/test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py` — new tests.\n\n## Testing\n- A `run_git_write` call whose first attempt fails with `unable to create temporary file: No\n  such file or directory` is retried and succeeds.\n- The macOS spelling (`... Invalid argument`) and the sibling markers are retried too.\n- A corrupt-object failure is NOT retried and surfaces immediately.\n- A signature that survives the whole bounded budget still returns its failing result.\n- `event_append._git_add` keeps its current behaviour after de-duplication.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `run_git_write` retries a write-side temp-file ENOENT/EINVAL failure — a test injects the\n      failure on the first attempt and asserts the call succeeds on retry.\n- [ ] The s3 doctor inherits it — a test drives a doctor git op through the seam with the fault\n      injected once and asserts the heal completes instead of raising `S3DoctorConflict`.\n- [ ] Corrupt-object signatures are still NOT retried — a test asserts immediate surfacing.\n- [ ] The write-side marker family has exactly one definition — a grep finds no second copy,\n      and `event_append`'s `git add` retry still passes its existing tests.\n- [ ] The full local gate set plus CI's pytest tiers pass.","id":"f7da-baae-3c93-47e2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Shared git seam does not retry write-side temp-file faults"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786601411942075001,"uuid":"5cb7204c-3640-4637-bb7d-dc90f051c591"}